    "slug": "design-in-memory-file-system",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "title": "Design In-Memory File System",
    "description": "Process [\"mkdir\",path], [\"addContentToFile\",path,text], [\"readContentFromFile\",path], and [\"ls\",path] on an empty filesystem rooted at /. mkdir creates missing parent directories. File writes append and require an existing parent directory. Reads name existing files. ls returns immediate child names in ASCII lexicographic order; on a file it returns only its basename. Mutations return null. Paths are absolute canonical paths with lowercase-letter components, no trailing slash except root; files and directories never conflict. At most 30 operations; paths contain at most 20 characters and each appended text contains at most 20 UTF-16 code units.",
    "difficulty": "hard",
    "concepts": ["hash-maps", "design"],
    "hints": ["Separate directories from file contents."],
    "attribution": "Original statement, examples, tests and solutions authored for Bekor, 2026. Uses a standard algorithmic pattern; no third-party exercise text used.",
